# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane): "Does the associativity
# axiom, evaluated as a real first-order logic:Formula over a concrete operation table,
# ENTAIL that both bracketings of (a·b)·c reach the same element?"  The op(x,y,z) atoms are
# fixed-arity n-ary predications the native reasoner reifies and joins; firing the law over
# the authored witness table DERIVES the binary consequent eq(assocWv, assocWv). That triple
# exists in the reasoned closure ONLY because the law fired — nothing asserts it. VALUES pins
# the query to the associativity witness so the answer is isolated from the other laws that
# also head on exa:eqRel. Over the closure the answer is exactly {assocWv}.
PREFIX exa: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/algebra/>

SELECT ?value WHERE {
    VALUES ?value { exa:assocWv }
    ?value exa:eqRel ?value .
}
